2. SKIP columns the database fills itself: IDENTITY / auto-increment primary keys, rowversion / timestamp, and audit columns (CreatedOnUtc, ModifiedOn, ...). Keep a nullable SubmissionId column OUT of the visible fields but INSIDE the INSERT (see rule 6).
3. TYPE MAP: nvarchar/varchar <=255 -> Text (name contains email -> Email, phone -> Composite preset phone); nvarchar(max)/ntext or >255 -> Textarea; int/bigint/decimal/money/float -> Number; date/datetime/datetime2 -> Date; bit -> Radio/Select with values 1 and 0 (NOT a Checkbox, see the token rules entry); char(2)/char(3) code columns -> Select over the lookup table when one is attached.
4. REQUIRED = NOT NULL without a default. A NOT NULL column with no field on the form makes every submit fail.
5. FOREIGN KEYS. A column named <Parent>Id / <Parent>_id / ParentId is a FK. Emit a Select whose VALUE is the parent primary key and whose LABEL is the parent name column, and set BOTH properties.optionsSource:"sql" AND properties.optionsSql — optionsSql alone renders an empty dropdown. Shape: {"key":"department_id","type":"Select","label":"Department","required":true,"properties":{"optionsSource":"sql","optionsSql":"SELECT Id AS value, Name AS label FROM [dbo].[MF_Test_Departments] ORDER BY Name"}}. The INSERT must bind the FK column to that field (:department_id) — never to the label text, or SQL Server rejects the row with a FK violation and the whole row is lost.
6. WIRE THE WRITE. Single form -> settings.databaseInsert = {enabled:true, connectionKey:"DashboardDatabase", databaseType:"SqlServer", insertSql:"INSERT INTO [dbo].[X](...) VALUES (...)", parameterMapping:{}}; app_batch form -> just set tableName. Always include the join-back column when the table has one: [SubmissionId] <- :_submissionId.
7. NEVER emit a databaseInsert whose target table does not exist — databaseInsert creates nothing. If the table is not in the attached-tables context, emit an app_batch with a CREATE TABLE entry instead.
8. SANITY: a form with 1-2 fields for a table with 8 columns is a bug, not a summary. Include every writable column; the user deletes extras in the Builder.',
  Tags = N'prompt_rule,sql,table,data-entry,databaseInsert,foreign-key,fk,select,optionsSql,ai-on-rails',
  Version = t.Version + 1, UpdatedOnDate = SYSUTCDATETIME()
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT
  (Slug, Kind, Title, Summary, Body, Tags, Examples, PortalId, Source, Version, CreatedOnDate)
  VALUES (N'sql-table-data-entry-form', N'prompt_rule',
          N'Data-entry form for an existing SQL table (including tables with foreign keys)',
          N'One input field per real column, FK columns become SQL-backed Selects on the parent table, and settings.databaseInsert writes the row on submit. A one-field form for a multi-column table is always wrong.',
          N'When the user asks for a form that WRITES INTO an existing table ("form nhap lieu cho bang X", "data entry form for table X", "create a form from the selected tables"), build a full data-entry form, not a lookup picker.

