GO

MERGE dbo.MF_AI_Knowledge AS t
USING (SELECT N'db-insert-token-rules' AS Slug, CAST(NULL AS INT) AS PortalId) AS s
  ON (t.Slug = s.Slug AND t.PortalId IS NULL)
WHEN MATCHED AND t.Source = 'megaform-builtin' THEN UPDATE SET
  Kind = N'prompt_rule',
  Title = N'insertSql token rules — composite sub-parts, multi-select values, auto-supplied tokens',
  Summary = N'A :token binds the submitted value of that field key. Composite sub-parts use :field.part, multi-selects arrive as a comma-joined string, and :_submissionId/:_formId/:_submittedOnUtc are supplied by the server.',
  Body = N'settings.databaseInsert.insertSql is a parameterised statement. Every :token is bound server-side to a submitted value — never string-concatenated — so wrapping a token in quotes ('':name'') is wrong and breaks the bind.

TOKEN -> VALUE
- :field_key binds the value submitted under that exact field key. parameterMapping is optional; use it only to point a token at a DIFFERENT field key ({":cust":"customer_name"}).
- COMPOSITE fields (type:"Composite" with widgetProps.preset name / name_plus / address / phone / dob / time) submit ONE combined value under the field key. To fill two columns from one composite, address the sub-part: VALUES (:name.first, :name.last). The server flattens the dot to an underscore (@name_first) and reads the raw part the renderer posts under __mf_parts. Requires MegaForm FormDatabaseInsert v20260726-01 or newer; on older builds a dotted token made SQL Server throw "Cannot call methods on nvarchar" (Msg 258) and the WHOLE row was silently dropped. Sub-part keys come from the preset: name -> first,last; name_plus -> prefix,first,middle,last,suffix; address -> street,city,state,zip; phone -> country,area,number,ext; dob -> day,month,year.
- Use :name (no dot) when the table has ONE full-name column. Never invent a dotted sub-part on a non-composite field — a scalar field has no parts and the token binds NULL.
- MULTI-SELECT fields (Checkbox and Chips) always submit an ARRAY, even with a single option ticked. The server joins them with ", " into one string. Map them to NVARCHAR wide enough for every option (>= 400 for interests/skills). NEVER map a Checkbox/Chips field to a BIT, INT or DATE column: an empty selection binds "" and the row fails. For a yes/no BIT column use a Radio/Select with values 1 and 0.
- AUTO-SUPPLIED: :_submissionId (identity of the MegaForm submission this row mirrors), :_formId, :_submittedOnUtc. Include [SubmissionId] <- :_submissionId whenever the table has that column so the custom row can be joined back to MF_Submissions.
- Date fields submit yyyy-MM-dd strings; that binds cleanly to date/datetime2. Number fields submit strings too — the column type does the conversion, so keep numeric columns numeric.

STATEMENT SHAPE — exactly ONE INSERT. No trailing second statement, no semicolon-stacking, no -- or /* */ comments: the server rejects the whole config. Bracket every identifier ([dbo].[Table], [Column]).

FAIL-SOFT WARNING: the custom-table write never blocks the submission. If the INSERT throws, the MegaForm submission still saves and the custom row is silently missing. So a wrong token type, a missing NOT NULL column or a FK violation shows up as "rows stopped appearing", not as an error. Use the builder Test INSERT button (dry-run inside a rolled-back transaction) after generating the SQL.',
  Tags = N'prompt_rule,databaseInsert,insertSql,token,composite,__mf_parts,multi-select,checkbox,chips,submissionId,ai-on-rails',
  Version = t.Version + 1, UpdatedOnDate = SYSUTCDATETIME()
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT
  (Slug, Kind, Title, Summary, Body, Tags, Examples, PortalId, Source, Version, CreatedOnDate)
  VALUES (N'db-insert-token-rules', N'prompt_rule',
          N'insertSql token rules — composite sub-parts, multi-select values, auto-supplied tokens',
          N'A :token binds the submitted value of that field key. Composite sub-parts use :field.part, multi-selects arrive as a comma-joined string, and :_submissionId/:_formId/:_submittedOnUtc are supplied by the server.',
          N'settings.databaseInsert.insertSql is a parameterised statement. Every :token is bound server-side to a submitted value — never string-concatenated — so wrapping a token in quotes ('':name'') is wrong and breaks the bind.

