MERGE dbo.MF_AI_Knowledge AS t
USING (SELECT N'premium-template-retarget-sql-table' AS Slug, CAST(NULL AS INT) AS PortalId) AS s
  ON (t.Slug = s.Slug AND t.PortalId IS NULL)
WHEN MATCHED AND t.Source = 'megaform-builtin' THEN UPDATE SET
  Kind = N'prompt_rule',
  Title = N'Retarget a premium template at an existing SQL table — fields change, the shell does not',
  Summary = N'Rename/retype the data fields to the table columns and wire settings.databaseInsert; never touch customHtml/customCss/theme and never drop the template Section steps.',
  Body = N'Retargeting a PREMIUM template at an existing SQL table ("make this form write into MF_Test_Employees", "sua form nay cho khop bang X") is a FIELD edit, never a design edit. The shell is frozen; the data model moves.

KEEP FROZEN — never emit these, they are re-asserted from the existing form on apply:
- settings.customHtml, settings.customCss, settings.theme, settings.templateGuideSlug.
- Every Section / Heading / Divider field. Those are the template STEPS and headings the shell paints and the wizard pages through; dropping premium_step_2..4 collapses a 4-step form to one page. They are restored automatically if omitted, but omit nothing.
- Row containers and their columns[] — the shell grid depends on them. Retype the fields INSIDE a Row, never the Row.

WHAT YOU DO CHANGE, per real column of the target table:
- key (rename to the column, snake_case), label, placeholder, required, helpText, options.
- type — Text -> Select / Date / Number / Composite is expected and is applied (scalar to scalar only).
- properties / widgetProps — for an FK column emit properties.optionsSource:"sql" AND properties.optionsSql (SELECT Id AS value, Name AS label FROM [dbo].[Parent]); for a phone column widgetProps.preset:"phone".
- Fields with no matching column: delete them. Their wrapper markup is removed from the shell automatically (a label with no input would otherwise linger).

ALSO WIRE THE WRITE: emit schema.settings.databaseInsert {enabled:true, connectionKey, databaseType:"SqlServer", insertSql, parameterMapping:{}} — databaseInsert and themeCssOverrides are the ONLY settings keys a premium edit may emit. Follow the insertSql token rules entry (composite sub-parts :name.first, multi-select CSV, :_submissionId join-back).

REBRAND COPY the shell hard-codes (hero title, step labels, section captions) with htmlTextSwaps [{find,replace}] where `find` is one of the SHELL TEXTS given verbatim — never by rewriting customHtml.',
  Tags = N'prompt_rule,premium,template,on-rails,sql,table,retarget,databaseInsert,section,steps,keep-style,ai-on-rails',
  Version = t.Version + 1, UpdatedOnDate = SYSUTCDATETIME()
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT
